-- Eleven weeks of training history for the four sample users, same rows as
-- the monolith's V23__seed_sample_activity_history.sql.
--
-- Why: V3 seeds only the last 7 days, so the dashboard month cards, the
-- month-over-month trend and the 12-week volume chart were empty or
-- degenerate (and all zero once the database outlived the month it was
-- seeded in). Rows are relative to NOW() like V3 and start one week before
-- the V3 activities (days 7..83), 3-4 sessions per week per user.
--
-- The rows use the identity (no fixed ids, so no h2/postgresql restart is
-- needed) and have no GPS streams: plain manual entries. Paces are slower
-- than the records seeded by V4 and no row fits a distance type V4 does not
-- cover, so PersonalRecordService.recalculateAllPRs() still produces the V4
-- rows (ActivityRepositoryTest guards this on H2).
--
-- INTERVAL '<n>' DAY / HOUR is the SQL-standard qualified form that runs on
-- both H2 (MODE=PostgreSQL) and PostgreSQL.

-- Pan (user 1): 39 activities, weeks 1-11 before the seeded week

-- John (user 2): 44 activities, weeks 1-11 before the seeded week

-- Jane (user 3): 44 activities, weeks 1-11 before the seeded week

-- Admin (user 4): 39 activities, weeks 1-11 before the seeded week
